    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n25192" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Jānĭcŭlum</span></b> ,
		i, n.
		Janus, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>one of the hills of Rome, on which Janus was said to have built
				a citadel</i>, <i><span class="en">Verg. A. 8, 358</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Ov. F. 1,
				245</span></i>; cf. <i><span class="en">Liv. 1, 33</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Mart. 4,
				64, 3</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Cic. Agr. 1, 5, 16</span></i>; <i><span class="en">2, 27,
			74</span></i>; <i><span class="en">id. Mil. 27, 74 al.</span></i>— Hence,
			</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Jānĭcŭlāris</span></b> ,
				e, <i>adj., of Janiculum</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">mons,</span>”
				i. e. <i>Janiculum</i>,
				 <i><span class="en">Serv. ad Verg. A. 6, 784</span></i>
			.</div>
